From 9199d745433e28875990ba0c9edc945f4c0a2c68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:18:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] vtest: add VCMD_SYNC_EXPORT_FD (protocol version 7)

Let a Venus vtest client export real sync_files for its syncs instead of
waiting for them on the CPU and handing out -1.

VCMD_SYNC_EXPORT_FD takes a sync id and value.  The server finds the
pending timeline submit that signals the sync to that value and asks the
context to export a fence for its ring:

- virgl_renderer_context_export_fence() and a new optional
  virgl_context::export_fence hook;
- the proxy skips the round trip when the fence already signaled, and
  otherwise sends RENDER_CONTEXT_OP_EXPORT_FENCE to the render server;
- vkr submits an empty batch with a SYNC_FD exportable VkFence to the
  ring's queue and returns vkGetFenceFdKHR(SYNC_FD).  Exporting resets the
  fence, so one fence per queue is reused.

The sync_file covers all work submitted to the ring so far, so it may
signal later than strictly needed, never earlier.  The reply is a status
(signaled / fd follows / unavailable) and the fd over SCM_RIGHTS.  When
an fd or 'signaled' is returned, the sync is detached from pending
submits, matching the copy-transference reset the client does next.

The render server and libvirglrenderer must come from the same build: an
older render server rejects the new op.

